      "http://localhost:11434/api/generate\n",
      "The capital of France is Paris. It'nerally considered as a global center for art, fashion, and culture. Established in the 3rd century BC by a Roman colonnade, it became one of Europe’s most important cities during the Middle Ages after being chosen to host French royalty starting with the Merovingian kings. The city was captured from the English during the Hundred Years' War and then taken back when Charles V abdicated in 1365 following defeat by Edward III at the Battle of Neville’s Cross on October 17, marking an end to England's territorial ambitions towards France; it is still a matter for historians. It also played a key role during French revolution with its storming and liberation in July-August 1789 when monarchy was overthrown by the public’s demand of “Liberty, equality and fraternity,” thus establishing republic as form of government which still stands today; it has been home to many famous artists such as Monet, Degas, Renoir amongst others.\n"
